art_114b6d12-10dc-482d-a3c5-a11f3c969f62_review_1	114b6d12-10dc-482d-a3c5-a11f3c969f62	review	[reject] - MT2 approach/description: the existing collision check (e.g. `const blocking = eating ? state.snake : state.snake.slice(0, -1);`) only excludes one vacated tail cell per tick. On the rotten-apple shrink branch (length>1), two tail cells vacate this tick (the normal per-step tail removal plus the extra rotten-shrink removal), so the blocking/self-collision set must exclude the last 2 segments (e.g. `state.snake.slice(0, -2)`) rather than 1. MT2's description/approach must explicitly state that the number of tail cells excluded from self-collision checking depends on the branch: 0 excluded when growing (ateFood), 1 excluded on a normal non-eating step, 2 excluded on ateRotten-shrink. Add an acceptance criterion with a concrete test case: a snake of length >=4 whose next head cell is the second-to-last tail segment eats a rotten apple, asserting gameOver is false (the move succeeds) rather than a false self-collision.	\N	2026-07-13 22:57:24.538572+00	\N
