art_114b6d12-10dc-482d-a3c5-a11f3c969f62_plan_v2	114b6d12-10dc-482d-a3c5-a11f3c969f62	plan	Add a second food type — a rotten apple — to the snake game. It spawns alongside the normal food in a different color/cell, and eating it shrinks the snake by one segment and subtracts 20 points (score floored at 0), then respawns on a free cell. If a length-1 snake eats a rotten apple, the game ends instead of shrinking below 1 segment. Normal food behavior (grow by 1, +10*newLength score) is unchanged. Self-collision checks must correctly account for how many tail cells vacate this tick depending on branch (0 growing, 1 normal step, 2 rotten-shrink).	\N	2026-07-13 22:58:51.285622+00	\N
