evt_2098b4fdf236	03f03cb4-8837-48dd-a7dc-ecb90d1d869d	2026-07-14 17:43:51.398257+00	human	hitl.decided	{"approval_id": "appr_4bf29ed5eeb6", "phase": "deploy", "decision": "approve", "reviewer": "cli-user", "notes": null, "commit_message": "Dashboard-triggered run\\n\\nObjective:\\nFirst Task: Add a score and a high score to the snake game\\r\\n\\r\\nRight now you can play but there's no score \\u2014 eating food does nothing visible. Add a score that goes up when the snake eats food, and show it on screen above the board.\\r\\n\\r\\nLonger snakes should be worth more: award points equal to 10 \\u00d7 the snake's length after it grows. So the first food (snake goes from 3 to 4) is worth 40, the next is 50, and so on. Score starts at 0 and resets when you hit New game.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlso track a high score: the best score reached during the current session. When a new game starts the score resets to 0 but the high score stays, and it updates whenever the current score passes it. For example, if you reach 90 and then start a new game, the high score stays 90 until you beat it. The high score is kept in memory only \\u2014 it does not need to survive a page reload. Show it next to the score.\\r\\n\\r\\nGrounding notes: \\"10 \\u00d7 length, first food = 40\\" seeds a score IOExample; \\"reach 90, new game, stays 90\\" seeds a highscore IOExample. Both pure-logic, node-testable. \\"In memory only, no page reload\\" explicitly fences off localStorage \\u2192 keeps coder out of the browser-API landmine.\\n\\nMicrotasks:\\n- Implement scoring logic in game engine\\n- Update game tests for scoring\\n- Implement score and high score UI\\n\\nFiles touched:\\n- .gitignore\\n- index.html\\n- package-lock.json\\n- src/game.js\\n- src/ui.js\\n- test/game.test.js\\n\\nRun: 03f03cb4-8837-48dd-a7dc-ecb90d1d869d"}	9199
