mt_1_game_logic	fc9e771d-664d-465d-888c-95add8286c5d	0	Implement scoring logic in game.js	Modify /workspace/repo/src/game.js to include score in the GameState. Update `newGame()` to initialize `score` to 0. Update `step()` so that if the snake eats food, the score increases by 10 times the snake's length after growth.	COMPLETED	1	[{"text": "newGame initializes score to 0", "examples": [{"given": {}, "expect": {"score": 0}}]}, {"text": "step increases score by 10 * new length when eating", "examples": [{"given": {"state": {"score": 0, "snake": [{"x": 1, "y": 1}, {"x": 1, "y": 2}, {"x": 1, "y": 3}]}, "eating": true, "newLength": 4}, "expect": {"score": 40}}, {"given": {"state": {"score": 40, "snake": [{"x": 1, "y": 1}, {"x": 1, "y": 2}, {"x": 1, "y": 3}, {"x": 1, "y": 4}]}, "eating": true, "newLength": 5}, "expect": {"score": 90}}]}, {"text": "step does not change score when not eating", "examples": [{"given": {"state": {"score": 40}, "eating": false}, "expect": {"score": 40}}]}]	[]	[".gitignore", "src/game.js"]	The Tester will call `newGame()` and `step()` with specific states to verify the score increments exactly as defined in the examples.	2026-07-14 18:01:42.119094+00	2026-07-14 18:01:59.738171+00	["/workspace/repo/src/game.js"]	1. Update `newGame` return object to include `score: 0`. 2. In `step`, identify the condition where the snake eats food (already handled by the `eating` boolean). 3. Calculate the new score: if `eating` is true, `newScore = state.score + (snake.length * 10)` (where `snake` is the updated snake array after growth); otherwise, `newScore = state.score`. 4. Return the `newScore` as part of the state object.	[]
